// Test: a for-loop body that pushes a value per iteration really does accumulate
// on the runtime stack -- `depth` observes 5 after five iterations.
//
// Note the static and dynamic models disagree here. The semantic validator treats
// the loop body as net-zero (it cannot know the trip count), so the accumulated
// values are unreachable by static means: adding five `print`s after the loop is
// rejected with "Type error in 'print': Stack underflow (requires 1 value)" even
// though the values are present at runtime. Only depth/clear and other dynamic
// ops can see them.
//
// Pinned deliberately: strict branch/loop stack-effect unification would make this
// an error outright, closing the gap. If that lands, this test should change or be
// removed as a conscious decision, not silently. See TODO.md, "Branch stack effects
// are not unified" -> blast radius.
//
// Different shape from for_loop_push_values.qd, whose body is net-zero (it prints)
// despite the name.
fn main() {
	0 5 1 for i {
		i
	}
	"depth: " print depth print nl
	clear
}
